  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Given the model $y=\\dfrac{k}{x^2}$, and that $y=5.1$ when $x=2.5$, find $k$, then calculate $y$ when $x=4.2$. Give $y$ correct to 3 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=31.875$; $y\\approx1.807$ (3 decimal places).",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5.1&=\\frac{k}{(2.5)^2}\\\\k&=5.1(2.5)^2\\\\k&=31.875\\\\y&=\\frac{31.875}{(4.2)^2}\\\\y&=\\frac{2125}{1176}\\\\y&\\approx1.807\\end{align*}$$\nThe value of $y$ is rounded to 3 decimal places.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 29
